{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554541-full-day-of-rest-meaning-for-kindred","id":1554541,"title":"\"Full Day of Rest\" Meaning for Kindred","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-21T09:10:16-07:00","id":1554541,"title":"\"Full Day of Rest\" Meaning for Kindred","content":"I apologize for such a simple question, but aggravated damage, &quot;... may be healed only with a full day of rest,&quot; and as a Storyteller, I was operating under the assumption that essentially, that meant the Kindred would have to remain in their haven for an entire 24 hours, resting, for however many levels of aggravated damage they received.<br /> <br /> However, it wasn't until recently I considered the idea that a &quot;full day of rest&quot; for a Kindred may mean their typical resting during the day. This latter idea has the benefit of not taking a character out of the chronicle just to ensure they are able to heal. This idea also aligns with the way healing aggravated wounds worked in earlier systems (1st and maybe 2nd?)<br /> <br /> Does anyone know which of the two mechanics is the intended one, and if my initial understanding was in fact, correct, any tips on how to not slow down the story by the temporary departure of a player character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28584-matter911","name":"Matter911","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-21T10:58:36-07:00","id":1554543,"title":"","content":"I think it's just a single sleep cycle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href